{
  "$comment": [
    "Single source of truth for every package the Creative Stack installs.",
    "Brewfile is GENERATED from this file (scripts/packages.py --emit brewfile);",
    "edit here, never there.",
    "",
    "Per package:",
    "  id        stable name used in logs and doctor output",
    "  provides  binaries that must exist afterwards; how we verify success.",
    "            Debian renames some (bat -> batcat), hence a list.",
    "  brew      Homebrew formula, or null if unavailable",
    "  cask      true when the brew entry is a cask (needs a GUI/sudo install)",
    "  arch      pacman package in core/extra, or null",
    "  aur       AUR package, tried when arch is null or pacman has no such name",
    "  debian    apt package, or null",
    "  fallback  language-ecosystem install used when no native package exists:",
    "            npm | uv | cargo | go | source | manual",
    "  gui       true = a desktop app; skipped under --profile headless",
    "  optional  true = a failure is a warning, not an error",
    "  early     true = sort to the front of the install list. Only matters on",
    "            the one-at-a-time retry pass, where it wins a race against a",
    "            dependency resolver (see jack) \u2014 not for ordering one package",
    "            ahead of another.",
    "",
    "Arch moves packages between extra and the AUR over time. scripts/packages.py",
    "treats every name as a hint: repo -> AUR -> fallback, and reports what it",
    "actually used. A stale name degrades to a warning, never a failed bootstrap."
  ],
  "npm_allow_scripts$comment": [
    "npm 12 does not run install scripts unless the package is named here, and",
    "it does not fail when it skips one \u2014 `npm install` prints 'added 2 packages'",
    "and exits 0 having left a package that cannot run. @anthropic-ai/claude-code",
    "is the visible case: its postinstall hardlinks the 240MB platform-native",
    "binary over a stub whose only job is to explain that the postinstall did not",
    "run. Arch ships npm 12 today and every distro will.",
    "",
    "An explicit list, not a blanket opt-in: allowing scripts is allowing",
    "arbitrary code at install time, so each name is here because a tool in this",
    "manifest does not work without it. Transitive dependencies have to be named",
    "too \u2014 npm matches the package running the script, not the one we asked for.",
    "packages.py warns when npm reports blocking something absent from this list."
  ],
  "npm_allow_scripts": [
    "@anthropic-ai/claude-code",
    "node-pty",
    "@github/keytar",
    "puppeteer"
  ],
